+### Rendering reference (wire → words)
+- Statuses: `queued`, `contact_initiated` (invite vs reminder via attempts-batch count; form
+  opened via `form_opened_at`), `form_completed`/`manual_recorded` → "Reference received",
+  `partial` → "Partially completed" + "answered {m} of {n}" (m = answered verification
+  fields, n = the slot's required set — derive from the verification block's non-null
+  fields; n is the slot's total field count from `result.gleam`'s per-slot sets),
+  `awaiting_correction`, `unreachable`, `refused`, `objected`, `skipped`, `failed`.
+- Verification field words: identity yes/no → "Yes"/"No"; tenancy/works-at yes/not_sure →
+  "Yes"/"No"/"Not sure"; payment record → "Always on time"/"Mostly on time"/"Often late"/
+  "Don't know"; property → "Excellent"/"Good"/"Fair"/"Poor"/"Didn't see it after"; notice →
+  "Yes"/"No"/"Ongoing"/"Don't know"; deposit → "In full"/"Partly"/"Withheld"/"Still held"/
+  "Don't know"; judgement questions → "Yes"/"No"/"Unsure"/"Prefer not to say"; as-stated
+  objects → "As stated"/the differs text/the stated text; amounts → euro string;
+  month-year → "As stated" style per §7.4 example ("As stated" is the wireframe's word for
+  confirmed periods — render the from/to as "As stated" only when the stored value equals
+  the application's stated value is NOT derivable client-side: render the stored from/to
+  verbatim instead; unanswered → "Not answered").
+- Attempts batches: group entries by `at`; batch 1 = "Invitation sent", batch 2 = single
+  delivered email = "Applicant asked to nudge", batches 3+ = "Reminder {n} sent"; channel
+  names joined "email + SMS". Skipped entries render as "Skipped — {detail}" (co-nudge
+  gate-skips show honestly as skipped lines with their reason).
+- What-happens-next: "Next reminder in ~2 days if there's no reply." (verbatim §7.4) while a
+  reminder is still pending (attempt batches < 3); no line after the final reminder
+  (honest — the §7.4 line would be false; the T+144h transition is silent).
+
